        "tool_execution_count": 0,
        "escalation": false,
        "final_response": "To authenticate with the Meridian API, you must send your secret API key in the `Authorization` header using bearer authentication [auth-05]. The key must be in the format `msk_live_...` or `msk_test_...` [auth-05].\n\nRules that always apply:\n\n- Secret keys (`msk_live_...`, `msk_test_...`) authenticate server-side requests and must never be exposed in browsers, mobile apps, or public repositories [auth-05].\n- Publishable keys (`mpk_live_...`) identify your account in front-end contexts and can only perform a small set of safe, read-mostly operations [auth-05].\n- A missing or malformed header returns `401` with error code `missing_authorization` [err-04].\n- An invalid or revoked key returns `401` with `invalid_api_key` [err-04].\n- A well-formed key that lacks permission for the operation returns `403` with `insufficient_scope` [err-04].\n\nMeridian does not support basic auth, query-string keys (`?api_key=...`), or cookies for the REST API [auth-05].\n\nSources: [auth-05], [err-04]",
